  {
    "id": "lock",
    "text": "Here's why it can't go wrong. The wallet is locked the moment the payment is recorded. A second check confirms it: automatically for small amounts, or with one tap from someone you trust. Then the contract on Arc works out the amount itself, and pays the locked wallet. Once. The agent signs through a Circle wallet. It never holds a key.",
